      <h2>About Me</h2>
      <p>
        I am Mohammad Abdullah — a writer, skeptic, and guitarist. I craft stories that dance on the edge of science and emotion. I've authored two thought-provoking novels: one diving into the <strong>pre-Big Bang cosmos</strong>, and another unraveling the <strong>scientific truth behind the theory of evolution</strong>. Through words, I challenge boundaries, question norms, and rebel against inherited beliefs.
      </p>
      <p>
        I also write <strong>short stories in Bengali</strong> that blend science, philosophy, and emotion — merging the cosmic with the personal, and the rational with the poetic.
      </p>
      <p>
        My guitar speaks when words fall short, and my skepticism fuels my journey through the universe of knowledge.
      </p>
