  <section class="ideology">
    <h2>My Ideology</h2>
    <p>
      I was born into a Muslim family, but my beliefs evolved beyond faith. I do not believe in a divine creator who remains silent in the face of human suffering. I’ve searched for him in wars, in genocides, in the cries of raped women, in starving children—and found only silence. I reject blind obedience to a god who watches but never acts. 
    </p>
    <p>
      I do not fear hell, for I do not believe in it. My morals come not from religion, but from empathy, reason, and humanity. I am an atheist who values evidence over emotion, science over superstition, truth over tradition. I believe religion should unite, not divide. I respect any belief system that promotes love, peace, and justice—including Sufism and Buddhism—but I rebel against dogma, violence, and manipulation in the name of God.
    </p>
    <p>
      My ideology is simple but firm: independent thought, scientific reasoning, universal compassion. I stand against all forms of inequality, discrimination, and imperialist exploitation. I support Palestinian rights and speak out against capitalist systems that deepen social injustice.
    </p>
    <p>
      I may be questioned, rejected, even hated. But I will never bow to fear or blind conformity. My path is mine. I choose knowledge, I choose logic, and above all — I choose freedom of thought.
    </p>
  </section>

